Juan, I was able to install rstan successfully using R 3.0.2. I also spent the time installing rstan 1.3.0, following the directions to uninstall 1.3.0 and then upgrading to 2.0.0.

Can you double check these files for modifications?
- Makevars
- Makeconf (R/etc/i386 or R/etc/x64)

The command used in my installation to compile stan.cpp is different from yours:
   g++ -m32 -I"C:/R/R-30~1.2/include"    -I"../inst/include/stansrc"   -I"../inst/include/stanlib/eigen_3.2.0"  -I"../inst/include/stanlib/eigen_3.2.0/unsupported"  -I../inst/include/stanlib/boost_1.54.0 -I"../inst/include"  -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE -DBOOST_DISABLE_ASSERTS   -I"C:/R/R-3.0.2/library/Rcpp/include" -I"d:/RCompile/CRANpkg/extralibs64/local/include"     -O3 -Wall  -mtune=core2   -c stanc.cpp -o stanc.o

If you look at it, there are different include directories that aren't present in your install.

One last thing -- can you uninstall whatever version you have, restart R, then try again? To uninstall (from within R):
library(rstan)
set_cppo('fast')
detach("package:rstan", unload = TRUE)
remove.packages('rstan')

