On Thursday, October 17, 2013 11:14:43 AM UTC-4, Juan Miguel Marin wrote:
> g++ -m32 -I"C:/R-30~1.2/include"    -I"../inst/include/stansrc"   -I""  -I"/unsupported"  -I -I"../inst/include"  -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE -DBOOST_DISABLE_ASSERTS   -I"C:/R-3.0.2/library/Rcpp/include" -I"d:/RCompile/CRANpkg/extralibs64/local/include"     -O3 -Wall  -mtune=core2   -c stanc.cpp -o stanc.o
> In file included from ../inst/include/stansrc/stan/gm/compiler.hpp:4:0,
>                  from stanc.cpp:5:
> ../inst/include/stansrc/stan/gm/ast.hpp:10:47: fatal error: boost/variant/recursive_variant.hpp: No such file or directory
> compilation terminated.
> make: *** [stanc.o] Error 1

I'm going to guess the culprit is

-I"d:/RCompile/CRANpkg/extralibs64/local/include"

Do you maybe have another (part of) boost in that directory? I think since it comes last, it is searched first so if there is some boost there, then it may be looking in the wrong place for its dependencies.

In general, can you try installing rstan after starting R with the --vanilla option?

Ben

