I have an MA model in https://github.com/euxoa/rutgers-snow, in files snowtrends.stan and snowtrends.R, and it is also much slower under 2.0.0 than it used to be under 1.3. Now 1000 samples takes something like 40 seconds instead of 5–10 seconds. Full mass matrix is in use. Initialization is deterministic (init=0). n_eff of the samples seem to be fine, though, or at least it's not much slower than it used to be.

