example.  As a bonus, I was now able to treate the top value as
censored instead of truncated.

So I guess my original "initial values" failure stemmed from the very
poor fit of the model.  Can you explain why stan seemed able to return
the gradient, even though it failed on evaluating initial values?

Estimations still seems to be struggling a bit; with 4500 sampling
iterations:
