Here's the relevant part of the likelihood, including the censoring
part:
    // mnDetail is in [1, 10]
    // We allow some probability (theta) of monogamy and then treat mnDetail-1
    // as poisson, with top-coding

    for (n in 1:N) {
        beta_x[n] <- (x[n] * beta)+alpha[iCluster[n]];

        if (mnDetail[n] == 1)
           increment_log_prob(log_sum_exp(bernoulli_log(1, theta),
	   bernoulli_log(0, theta) + poisson_log(0, exp(beta_x[n]))));
        else {
           increment_log_prob(bernoulli_log(0, theta) +
	   poisson_log(mnDetail[n]-1, exp(beta_x[n])));
