On Saturday, October 19, 2013 8:38:33 PM UTC+3, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> > (But my experience is limited.) I even fail to see why the sampler gets stuck with small values of the scales.
>
> Lower scale restricts the movements of lower-level parameters.

Ok, so the funnel arises from another term in the log posterior. There is no sum over data there, so it is not as steep as a "low-level funnel" would be, but it may be steep enough, especially if the whole hyperparameterstructure is quite weak and in that sense independent (from lower-level likelihood), as mine is.

Thanks.

