I am in the process of implementing a zero-inflated ordered probit model with correlated errors (ZIOPC). I was able to adapt the zero inflated Poisson model found in the rstan manual to zero inflated ordered logit and probit models, but am stuck on this last step of allowing the errors to be correlated. Syntactically, the key difference is that the ZIOPC model requires transformed parameters. I'm finding that once the transformed parameter section is included, only one more variable--of any kind--can be declared in either the transformed parameters or in the model section. (And I don't see anything obvious, like missing semi-colons on the preceding line.)

Anyhow, I was just wondering whether anyone had figured out a solution to this problem. (I agree that this is not a Macs vs Linux problem since I am using a PC.) I am still using rstan 1.3 because I read that the kinks were still being worked out of rstan 2.0, but if anyone knows whether upgrading would do the trick, I would be happy to do so. Otherwise, I can send my code.

All best,

Pete

