On Saturday, October 19, 2013 8:38:33 PM UTC+3, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> What's the effective sample/second rate?

I ran some tests, 10 rounds of a chain of length 5000, with init=0. The numbers below are effective samples in seconds,
geometric mean over all parameters:

v. 1.3:
26.374786 14.228899 17.098531 17.192325  8.579270  4.856640 27.983170 31.880291  3.649093 12.654570

v. 2.0:
6.205991  3.625549 11.833662  5.664172  2.750165  3.945409 11.089825 10.332482  7.389430 10.348843

There is huge variation across chains, but v. 1.3 seems to be faster. I have no multivariate normals. In hindsight, geometric mean is a bad summary statistic. The geometry of the model is bad. I'll run the tests again with a better geometry soon.

