Prequel 1: sometimes it might be useful to try non-default sampler parameters (see: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/Fl3RBPscUXo)
Prequel 2: one could merge chains coming from different algorithms and/or iter/warmup/thin settings (as long as n_save and warmup2 are equal) and/or "controls", as they are named now (see: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/sCLQYj02tB8)

So I'm writing/rewriting some rstan functions. A few examples follow.

Let sm be a compiled stan model.

> iter <- c(10, 100, 500)
> warmup <- c(5, 50, 250)
> thin <- c(1, 10, 50)
> algorithm <- c("HMC", "NUTS", "NUTS")
> control <- list(list(adapt_delta = 0.61, int_time = 3 * pi,
+                      metric = "unit_e", stepsize = 0.6),
+                 list(adapt_delta = 0.62, max_treedepth = 12,
+                      metric = "unit_e", stepsize = 0.7),
+                 list(adapt_delta = 0.63, max_treedepth = 15,
+                      metric = "diag_e", stepsize = 0.5))
> sflist <- mclapply(1:3, mc.cores = detectCores(),
+                    function(i) sampling(sm, chains = 1, chain_id = i, seed = 12345,
+                        iter = iter[i], warmup = warmup[i], thin = thin[i],
+                        algorithm = algorithm[i], control = control[[i]]))
> sf <- sflist2stanfit(sflist)

I'd love to add a fourth case, but setting metric = dense_e doesn't work now (https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/AJXmiruMiSA).

I'd like to look at something like:

> get_sampler_config(sf)
chain_id                1      2      3
algorithm             HMC   NUTS   NUTS
- int_time           9.42     NA     NA
- max_treedepth        NA     12     15
- metric               NA unit_e diag_e
- stepsize             NA   0.70   0.50
- stepsize_jitter      NA   0.00   0.00
iter                   10    100    500
warmup                  5     50    250
thin                    1     10     50
Adaptation:
- engaged            TRUE   TRUE   TRUE
- gamma              0.05   0.05   0.05
- delta              0.61   0.62   0.63
- kappa              0.75   0.75   0.75
- t0                10.00  10.00  10.00

I can now notice that metric and stepsize are not changed when algorithm is "HMC", but it'll be soon fixed.
Otherwise:

> sampler_config <- get_sampler_config(sf, print = FALSE)
> sampler_config
  chain_id sampler int_time max_treedepth metric stepsize stepsize_jitter iter
