Hmmm, without looking at the data or anything else more closely, from your model the Conceptions data has a lower bound of zero, making it possible that impConceptions[n] could be zero.  That may not happen with your data but it's possible with the model definition

Also, another possibility is that I'm not sure how we're handling the boundary cases with truncation.  I.E., if impConceptions[n] == 1 or == 15, what happens.  One quick test for this would be to do the truncation for T[0,16] or something like that just as a test.

Cheers,
Marcus

