Hi Stan users,

I am in the early stages of attempting to migrate from JAGS to STAN - and so far love STAN.  Nevertheless I am having difficulty with negative binomial models. I just don't seem to be able to parameterize them correctly.  Below I have provided an R script that encapsulates a small example data set along with glm, JAGS and STAN code (I apologize if it is too long).  The negative binomial section is between the two bold headings...
Along with two attempts to model NB in STAN (last two blocks of code), I have provided the frequentist, JAGS and STAN for Poisson and NB - mainly to clarify the model I am attempting to fit.  I have also included some embedded output (in blue).

Any advice that can be offered for constructing the negative binomial within STAN would be greatly appreciated.

## Generate some data (ANCOVA-like)
## - y: an integer response
## - fact: a categorical factor with three levels
## - x: a continuous covariate
set.seed(1)
fact <- gl(3,10,30)
x <- rnorm(30,0,5)
Xmat<-model.matrix(~fact+x)
int <- 10
eff1<-5
eff2 <- 10
slope <- 1
mu <- Xmat %*% c(int,eff1,eff2,slope)
mu[mu<0]<-0
disp <- 3 #size/shape
prob <- disp/(disp+mu) #prob
y <- rnbinom(30,disp,prob)
data <- data.frame(y=y,x=x,fact=fact)

##visualize the data (can skip this step)
library(ggplot2)
ggplot(data,aes(y=y, x=x, colour=fact))+geom_point()+geom_smooth(method="lm")

## Poisson=============================================================

## glm------------------------------------------------------------------
(coefs <- glm(y~fact+x, family="poisson")$coef)
#(Intercept)       fact2       fact3           x
# 2.21421375  0.24894914  0.64061383  0.04783587
exp(coefs %*% t(model.matrix(~gl(3,1,3)+rep(0,3))))
#            1        2        3
#[1,] 9.154209 11.74189 17.37144

## jags ---------------------------------------------------------------
jagsString="
model {
  for (i in 1:n){
    Y[i] ~ dpois(mu[i])
    log(mu[i]) <- max(-20, min(20, eta[i]))
    eta[i]<-inprod(beta[],X[i,])
  }
  for (i in 1:4) {
    beta[i] ~ dnorm(0,1.0E-06)
  }
}
"
writeLines(jagsString, con="model.jags")
X <- model.matrix(~fact+x)
data.list <- with(fish.OS.site, list(Y=y, X=X, n=length(y)))
model.jags <- jags(data.list,inits=NULL, parameters.to.save=c("beta"),
                   model.file="model.jags",n.chain=3,n.iter=100000, n.burnin=2000, n.thin=50)
#plot(as.mcmc(model.jags))
#autocorr.diag(as.mcmc(model.jags))
print(model.jags)
